@startuml k9x_studio_activity_flow_v2

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C060
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title K9X StudioX — Spec Import Activity Flow v2.0\n(running on the published k9-aif package — studio_core / studio_agents own the SBB/ABB layer)

|User / Browser|
start

:Upload spec doc (.docx/.pdf/.md)\nPOST /spec/import;

|FastAPI (thin layer)|
:backend/api/routes.py\nreceive HTTP request;
:from studio_core.router.router_factory\n  import route_event;
:route_event("spec_import", payload);

|studio_core.router.K9EventRouter|
:route(event_type = "spec_import");
note right
  K9EventRouter --|> k9_aif_abb.k9_core
                    .router.BaseRouter
  Deterministic dispatch — event_type
  resolved to its registered orchestrator,
  called in-process (no Kafka in Phase 2)
end note
:Dispatch → SpecImportOrchestrator;

|SpecImportOrchestrator|
:_load_squad("SpecImportSquad")\n(AgentRegistry + SquadLoader, both\nimported live from k9_aif_abb);
:squad.execute_flow(payload);

|SpecImportSquad  (flow defined in squads/yaml/spec_import_squad.yaml)|

:**GovernanceAgent**\nscreens doc for safety/PII\n→ result_key: governance;
if (governance.passed == true?) then (yes)
else (no — every later step's\n`when:` evaluates false)
  :Squad returns with governance.passed = false;
  |SpecImportOrchestrator|
  :publish_status("FlowBlocked");
  :Return blocked response\n(never reaches parser/LLM/canvas);
  |FastAPI (thin layer)|
  :Return error to UI;
  stop
endif

:**SpecParserAgent**\n(extends studio_agents.parallel\n.K9SubAgentSpawner)\n→ result_key: parsed;
note right
  spawn_parallel([
    IntakeExtractorAgent,
    AgentExtractorAgent,
    ZoneMappingAgent
  ])
  ThreadPoolExecutor — concurrent,
  merged back into shared context.
  K9SubAgentSpawner supplies the
  mechanics only; SpecParserAgent
  owns which children + how to merge.
end note
fork
  :[sub] IntakeExtractorAgent\nproject name, domain, description;
fork again
  :[sub] AgentExtractorAgent\nagent table from spec §3.1.8;
fork again
  :[sub] ZoneMappingAgent\nzone → component mapping\n(GREEN/AMBER/RED);
end fork
:Merge sub-agent results\ninto `parsed` context;

:**LLMGroupingAgent**  (AMBER — LLM call)\nproposes a squad grouping\n→ result_key: llm_grouping;
:**ScoringAgent**  (GREEN)\nscores LLM grouping vs.\nrule-based zone grouping,\npicks the winner\n→ result_key: scored;
:**CanvasBuilderAgent**  (GREEN)\nbuilds canvas-suggestion JSON\n(nodes + edges for React Flow)\n→ result_key: canvas;

|SpecImportOrchestrator|
:Collect squad result;
:publish_status("FlowCompleted");

|FastAPI (thin layer)|
:Return canvas suggestion JSON;

|User / Browser|
:Canvas auto-populates with\nsuggested architecture;
:User reviews / edits\nvia Inspector;
note right
  v2.0 change vs. Phase-2 draft: studiox now
  depends on the published k9-aif package
  (pip install k9-aif, requirements.txt) for
  BaseRouter / BaseOrchestrator / BaseAgent /
  BaseSquad / SquadLoader / AgentRegistry.
  studiox's own SBB/ABB extensions live in
  studio_core/ and studio_agents/ — renamed
  from k9_core/ and k9_agents/, which collided
  with the framework's internal package names.
end note
stop

@enduml
